# Context filter for `docker build -f transport-sentinel/Dockerfile .`
#
# BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the context root's
# .dockerignore, so this file must be self-sufficient rather than an addition
# to the root one. It is a superset of it.
#
# The line that matters is `**/node_modules`. The runtime stage runs
# `npm ci --omit=dev` and then copies `transport-sentinel/api/` over the
# result; without this, a developer's local `api/node_modules` — the full dev
# tree, ~91MB — is in the context, lands on top of the production install and
# ships in the image.

node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
coverage
**/coverage
.git
.github
.gitignore
docs
**/*.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
npm-debug.log*
**/.DS_Store

# The other consoles. Only packages/ and transport-sentinel/ are ever copied,
# but excluding them keeps the context small and the build fast.
agro-sentinel
cash-sentinel
cognitex-landing
industry-sentinel
personal-sentinel
productivity-sentinel
services
